From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qrb2210-arduino-imola: attach MPM to the
 cluster power domain

agatti.dtsi makes the MPM the parent power domain of cluster_pd, but the
MPM driver registers no genpd provider: it consumes the cluster domain
and programs wakeups from a GENPD_NOTIFY_PRE_OFF notifier, as the binding
describes. The subdomain link can never resolve, so cpuidle-psci-domain
defers forever and, because each attempt re-registers providers, the
retries never settle and the root filesystem is never mounted.

Invert the link for this board as qcom,mpm.yaml documents.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [qcom-next snapshot without the irq-qcom-mpm power-domain provider; drop once linux-qcom-next has it]
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola.dts
@@ -231,6 +231,14 @@
 	no-map;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The MPM driver consumes the cluster power domain (see qcom,mpm.yaml) rather
+ * than providing one, so the cluster domain cannot take it as its parent.
+ */
+&cluster_pd {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+};
+
 &gpi_dma0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
@@ -335,6 +343,11 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&mpm {
+	/delete-property/ #power-domain-cells;
+	power-domains = <&cluster_pd>;
+};
+
 &pm4125_vbus {
 	regulator-min-microamp = <500000>;
 	regulator-max-microamp = <500000>;
